    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **BUILD SUCCESS**, 2 tests run, 0 failures.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the locality derivation so it prefers the postcode, falling back to the city table.\n\n**`OwnerLocality.java`** \u2014 added:\n- A `REGION_POSTCODES` table (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099).\n- A new public `forPostcodeAndCity(postcode, city)` that looks up the region by postcode range first, and only falls back to `forCity(city)` when the postcode is absent, non-numeric, or in no known range.\n- A private `forPostcode(...)` helper returning `null` when the postcode doesn't resolve (so the fallback triggers).\n- Kept `forCity(...)` unchanged, since `OwnerRestControllerV1` still uses it for postcode validation.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `locality` mapping now calls `OwnerLocality.forPostcodeAndCity(owner.getPostcode(), owner.getCity())` instead of `forCity(owner.getCity())`.\n\nThis returns the same region for the known cities (e.g. Sydney + 2000 \u2192 NSW) but disambiguates via postcode: an unknown city with a VIC-range postcode (3000) now yields VIC, as the new acceptance test `functionalityPostcodePreferredOverCity` asserts.",
