    "probe_text": "The `POST /api/owners` endpoint is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:176-214`). Here is everything it applies, in execution order. I've tagged each as **[V]** validation (can reject the request) or **[S]** side-effect (mutation, persistence, or logging).\n\n### Ordered sequence\n\n1. **[V] Authorization** (`@PreAuthorize` on the method) \u2014 caller must hold role `OWNER_ADMIN`, else 403.\n\n2. **[S] Normalize address on the incoming DTO** (line 179, `AddressNormalizer.normalize`) \u2014 trims, collapses internal whitespace to single spaces, upper-cases, and expands whole-word abbreviations `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`. `null`/blank becomes `\"\"`. This mutated value is what the required-field check below sees.\n\n3. **[V] Required-fields check** (line 180, `validateRequiredFields`) \u2014 `firstName`, `lastName`, `address` (in its normalized form), `city`, and `telephone` must each be non-blank. Any missing ones are collected and thrown together as `MissingOwnerFieldsException` \u2192 400 with an `errors` array. (Email and postcode are *not* required here.)\n\n4. **[V] Postcode check** (line 181, `validatePostcode`) \u2014 if a postcode was supplied (blank/absent is allowed): it must be exactly 4 digits, and if the city maps to a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD via `OwnerLocality.forCity`) the value must fall within that region's inclusive range. Otherwise `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` \u2192 400 (`errors: [postcode]`). An unknown region accepts any 4-digit code.\n\n5. **[S] Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** entity (line 183).\n\n6. **[S] + [V] Normalize telephone** (line 184, `TelephoneNormalizer.normalize`) \u2014 strips spaces/dashes/brackets, canonicalizes to E.164 (`+` and 8\u201315 digits; assumes `+61` and drops a leading `0` when no `+`). Also validates: rejects if not E.164, or if the national-number length is wrong for a fixed-plan country code (`+61`\u21929 digits, `+1`\u219210) \u2192 `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` 400 (`telephone`). The normalized value replaces the field.\n\n7. **[S] + [V] Normalize email** (line 185, `normalizeEmail`) \u2014 if non-blank, must match the email pattern else `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` 400 (`email`); the accepted value is lower-cased and stored. Blank/null is left untouched.\n\n8. **[S] Default the registration date** (lines 186-188) \u2014 if `registrationDate` is null, set it to `LocalDate.now()` (today).\n\n9. **[S] Roll registration date to a business day** (line 189, `toBusinessDay`) \u2014 Saturday/Sunday is advanced to the following Monday; a weekday is kept. All later date-based logic uses this adjusted date.\n\n10. **[S] Set `householdId`** (line 190, `HouseholdNormalizer.householdId`) \u2014 a SHA-256-derived hex id computed from the normalized (trimmed/whitespace-collapsed/lower-cased) last name + address.\n\n11. **[S] Set `identityKey`** (lines 191-192, `buildIdentityKey`) \u2014 `normalizedTelephone + \"|\" + (email or \"\") + \"|\" + (householdId only if the request set `sharesHousehold`, else \"\")`.\n\n12. **[V] Duplicate-owner check** (line 193, `rejectDuplicateOwner`) \u2014 scans all existing owners; if any has the same `identityKey`, throws `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` \u2192 409.\n\n13. **[V] City capacity check** (lines 194-196) \u2014 if the city already holds \u2265 `CITY_OWNER_LIMIT` (50) owners (case-insensitive count), throws `OwnerCityFullException` \u2192 409.\n\n14. **[V] Daily registration limit** (lines 197-200) \u2014 counts owners already registered on this owner's (business-day-adjusted) `registrationDate`; if \u2265 `DAILY_OWNER_LIMIT` (100), throws `OwnerDailyLimitException` \u2192 429.\n\n15. **[S] Compute `bulkSignupWarning`** (line 201) \u2014 `true` when that same-day count is > `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD` (80). (Reported on the response DTO, not persisted.)\n\n16. **[S] Set `customerCode`** (line 202, `buildCustomerCode`) \u2014 `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where NNNN is one more than the current count of owners in that city.\n\n17. **[S] Set `namesakeCount`** (line 203) \u2014 count of existing owners sharing the same first+last name (case-insensitive), i.e. namesakes *before* this insert.\n\n18. **[S] Set `householdSize`** (line 204) \u2014 count of existing owners sharing the `householdId`, plus one.\n\n19. **[S] Persist the owner** (line 205, `clinicService.saveOwner`) \u2014 the actual insert (assigns the id).\n\n20. **[S] Audit log** (lines 206-208) \u2014 writes an `AUDIT` logger `info` record with id, customerCode, registrationDate, and computed `MembershipLevel.forOwner(owner)`.\n\n21. **[S] Build the response** (lines 209-213) \u2014 map to `OwnerDto`, set its `bulkSignupWarning`, set the `Location` header to `/api/owners/{id}`, return **201 Created**.\n\n### Notes\n- The **V2** controller (`OwnerRestControllerV2`) only exposes a paged *list* endpoint \u2014 it has no create \u2014 so all creation logic lives in V1 above.\n- Several validations run *after* mutations/normalizations, but since the whole method executes within a single request and `saveOwner` is the only persistence call (step 19), a validation failure at steps 12\u201314 aborts before anything is written. Note, however, that `addOwner` is **not** annotated `@Transactional` (unlike `deleteOwner`), so it relies on there being a single save rather than on transactional rollback."
